 ],
 "description": "The jabberwock's graph-native chain (designed by it, no new Rust primitive): recognise the nav game from the world's framework/affordances -> build the SpatialLocation map from the cells + the world's `neighbour` lattice (floor by figure/ground, NOT a Python heuristic) -> engage routing via one `operates_in` edge that cascades through the standing autonomy + enact + routing machinery -> learn walls by bumping (Boundary blocks + Impasse surprised_by). The world only provides cells, the lattice, and the affordances; every decision here is graph data on the agent's own tick.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "arc3_navigation",
  "description": "perceive cells -> recognise navigation game -> build map -> route avatar to goal_cell -> learn walls -> understand. All rules on tick."
 },
